   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_step300_physics_column",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay_physics=1 (sfclayrev) sf_surface_physics=1 (slab) bl_pbl_physics=1 (YSU), data/eqwefic/scm_ref) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork: at the PHYSICS-DRIVER level (commit 592f693, module_esm_dump hooks around radiation_driver, surface_driver + pbl_driver and the physics-tendency sum in dyn_em/module_first_rk_step_part1.F; dumps subassembly_rad/_pbl/_all at step 300, column its of row jps) and at the KERNEL level for the same step (sfclayrev scm_ref_600.json, RRTM scm_ref2_600.json with the in-kernel internals, Dudhia scm_ref_600.json). All references are real32 model values, so the contract is rel 1e-5 (CLAUDE.md), widened where documented. This document runs the WHOLE column physics of the step except the land-surface scheme: RRTM longwave (RRTMColumn -> RRTMSetcoef -> RRTMGasOptics -> RTRNSweep -> RRTMLWHeating) and Dudhia shortwave give rthraten = dthdt_lw + dthdt_sw; the revised MM5 surface layer (SfclayRev) gives u*, fm, fh, Ri_b, wind speed, 10 m wind and z0; YSU receives those and rthraten and gives the boundary-layer tendencies; every stage is fed through variable_map/param_to_var edges into `<x>_in` coupling-target parameters (the mount-edge libraries lower the components' `input_<x>` rewrite targets to them), and only the column state of the step, the surface scalars and the slab's fluxes are prescribed. Tolerances: surface-layer fluxes and profile functions rel 5e-05 and the Ri_b-derived stability quantities (psim, psih, br, rmol, flhc) rel 1e-04 (1e-6 where exact) -- the references are the real32 model's own outputs, and at this regime the real32 kernel differs from its real64 replay by up to 5.3e-5 (rmol, psim; the stable regime amplifies real32 roundoff in theta_v1 - theta_vs through the bulk Richardson number), so unlike the components' own tests (real64 references, rel 2e-5) the assembly tolerances follow the real32 floor; PBL height rel 5e-05 (the surface layer's residuals propagate into YSU's bulk-Richardson height search: measured 3.3e-5), kpbl and regime exact, K_h/K_m Linf abs 5e-3 m^2/s (real32 dump), longwave fluxes Linf abs 5e-3 W/m^2 and dthdt_lw/rthraten Linf abs 2e-8 K/s (the RRTM end-to-end contract: the sweep consumes the gas optics' quantised ITR, exact up to +/-1 flips), dthdt_sw Linf 1e-9 K/s (binary64 roundoff), gsw/glw/olr rel 2e-5. The PBL TENDENCIES and rth_phys_sum are asserted against the dt -> 0 LIMIT of the YSU kernel, which is what this assembly evaluates, and NOT against WRF's driver-level rthblten/rublten/rvblten/rqvblten: those are the IMPLICIT tridiagonal step's (c_new - c_old)/dt at dt = 60 s and are not instantaneous derivatives -- at this step size they differ from one by 1.2 % (theta), 4.0 % (u), 2.1 % (v) and 0.8 % (q_v) of the column maximum. The reference is the second-order Richardson extrapolation (8 T(dt/4) - 6 T(dt/2) + T(dt))/3 of real64 replays of THIS step's dumped YSU column through kernels/ysu_driver of the ctessum-claude/WRF fork at dt = 0.04/0.02/0.01 s (data/eqwefic/dumps/ysu/scmref_600_dt*.json, transcribed by tools/reref_pbl_dt0.py), the same reference components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu/ysu.esm's own tests use; the kernel carries NEED_B4B_DURING_CCPP_TESTING = 1, so ttnp is a TEMPERATURE tendency and the theta reference is ttnp/pi2d (FORTRAN_BUGS N1). The extrapolation is self-consistent to 7.3e-10 (utnp) and 3.6e-8 (ttnp) of the column maximum when recomputed from dt = 0.08/0.04/0.02. THIS DOCUMENT IS THE CLEANEST CHECK OF THAT CLAIM IN THE REPO, because it feeds YSU the DUMPED geometry rather than a computed one: the measured residuals are dtheta/dt 7.06e-9 K/s, du/dt 6.21e-9 and dv/dt 8.70e-9 m/s^2, dqv/dt 4.93e-12 1/s and rth_phys_sum 4.43e-9 K/s, i.e. about 1e-5 of the column maxima, against 1.9e-6, 1.5e-5, 3.5e-6 and 5.2e-10 before. The tolerances are 4x those measured values. The slab land-surface scheme is NOT co-mounted (its 4-layer soil column shares the column_nonuniform_1d axis lev at a different size and esm index sets are document-scoped, PLAN.md gap (n)), so the fluxes YSU receives are the slab's driver-level values prescribed as hfx_lsm/qfx_lsm, while sfc_hfx/sfc_qfx are the surface layer's own values checked against the kernel dump; the driver-level th2/t2/q2 are overwritten by the land-surface branch of surface_driver, so those three are referenced to the kernel-level sfclayrev dump. Regime: step 300 (00:00 UTC = 17:34 LST, sunset, coszen < 0 so gsw = 0 and dthdt_sw = 0), stable land column: slab hfx = -19.1 W/m^2 (sfclayrev's own -19.13), Ri_b = 0.058 (regime 1), u* = 0.208 m/s, h = 556 m, kpbl = 10, thin cirrus (qi <= 1.7e-6), glw = 264, olr = 239 W/m^2.",
